// CONTRACT (must-error): an if-expression with one VOID arm and one value arm joins to
// `void | i32`, and no value has that type. The annotated spelling already reports it
// (`cannot assign void | i32 to 'xe' of type i32`), so the value slots that infer their
// demand read the same rule: a type that MENTIONS void carries an arm with no value, and a
